# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values, if you need to point the
# frontend at something other than its default local dev target. Read by
# Vite at build time (import.meta.env.VITE_*) — see the README's
# "Environment variables" section.
#
# The default (api/http.ts) already matches the backend's own default
# PORT, so local development needs no .env file here at all — this file
# exists mainly to document the one variable that exists, and as a
# template for a production deployment (Vercel), where it's set to the
# deployed API's real URL.

VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
